  <title>On-screen speech display</title>
  <p>
    The on-screen speech display shows Orca's speech output and provides a history of recent
    speech.
  </p>
  <p>
    Application developers can use the window to examine Orca's speech output visually while
    testing their applications. It also provides a history of recent speech for review and
    copying.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-on-screen-speech-display">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Speech</gui> category, <gui>On-Screen Display</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Font size</gui>: Sets the text size in the
          on-screen speech display. Default: 14. Range: 8 to 72.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Text color</gui>: Sets the text color in
          the on-screen speech display. Default: #ffffff.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Background color</gui>: Sets the
          background color in the on-screen speech display. Default: #000000.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
  <section id="commands-on-screen-display">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Speech and verbosity</gui> group.
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Toggle the on-screen speech display on and off</gui>: <keyseq>
            <key>Orca Modifier</key>
            <key>Shift</key>
            <key>D</key>
          </keyseq>
        </p>
        <p>
          Opens or closes the speech display. It includes recent speech even if the window was
          closed at the time. Select text and use <keyseq>
            <key>Ctrl</key>
            <key>C</key>
          </keyseq>
          to copy it for pasting into another application.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
